{{also|talkshop}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{rfe|en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive|informal}} To [[discuss]] one's [[work]], [[business]], [[profession]], [[vocation]]{{,}} or ''(sometimes, by extension)'' [[avocation]]; especially, to do so in a way that only [[insider]]s ([[initiate#English:_one who is knowledgeable and experienced in a topic|initiates]]) would understand, that is [[tedious#Adjective|tedious]] or [[boring#Adjective|boring]] to the [[listener]], or both.

====Usage notes====
* This is an idiomatic instance of a general construction consisting of ''[[talk]]'' with the topic area as object of the verb. One can ''talk baseball'', ''talk philosophy'', or ''talk trash''.

====Related terms====
* {{l|en|shop talk|pos=n}}

